A trailing * matches the rest of the path (Requirement 7.1).
Not pinned by the spec, so not tested: whether /files or /files/ match, and
whether the matched rest is exposed in req.params.

### one segment
GET /files/readme.txt
=> 200

{"path": "/files/readme.txt"}

### several segments
GET /files/crypt/north/bones.json
=> 200

{"path": "/files/crypt/north/bones.json"}

### a different prefix doesn't match
GET /tombs/readme.txt
=> 404

{"error": "ROUTE NOT FOUND IN THIS REALM"}
